# === AI / Tooling ===
# `.claude/skills/` is shared project convention and IS committed. Everything else
# under .claude/ is local machine state: settings.local.json, locks, scheduled-task
# bookkeeping. Note the `*` — git does not descend into an ignored directory, so
# `/.claude/` without it would make the negations below unreachable.
/.claude/*
!/.claude/skills/
# settings.json IS committed: it declares the roadkeep marketplace and enables the
# plugin, so a clone gets the hook, the tools and the skill without any local setup.
!/.claude/settings.json
# hooks/ IS committed: the plugin never installs on Claude Code on the web (no
# `/plugin`), so the committed roadkeep-launch.py is how a cloud session gets the
# guard the plugin would give a local machine.
!/.claude/hooks/

# Python bytecode. `.claude/hooks/` holds the roadkeep guard hook, so running it
# leaves `__pycache__/` beside the source. Bytecode restates a file already tracked
# next to it, cannot be reviewed, and is per-interpreter.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Build output
dist/
storybook-static/
.sb-test/

# IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Environment
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# TypeScript build info
*.tsbuildinfo

# Vitest browser-mode failure screenshots.
__screenshots__/
.vitest-attachments/
